# Project: Form Component Development Standards

## Form Component Overview

Form components in Typerefinery follow a standardized architecture pattern that ensures consistency, maintainability, and integration with the form system, Flow API, and client-side data collection.

**Base Component**: `typerefinery/components/forms/field`  
**Location**: `/apps/typerefinery/components/forms/fields/`  
**Reference**: See `docs/forms/developer-guide.md` for comprehensive development guide

## Core Architecture Principles

### 1. Inheritance via Resource Super Type

**MANDATORY**: All form field components MUST extend `typerefinery/components/forms/field` via `sling:resourceSuperType`.

```json
{
  "isContainer": false,
  "group": "Typerefinery - Forms",
  "sling:resourceType": "ws:Component",
  "sling:resourceSuperType": "typerefinery/components/forms/field",
  "description": "Component description",
  "title": "Component Title"
}
```

**Rules:**
- **REQUIRED**: `sling:resourceSuperType` must be `"typerefinery/components/forms/field"`
- **REQUIRED**: `group` must be `"Typerefinery - Forms"` to appear in form component palette
- **REQUIRED**: `isContainer` should be `false` unless component needs to contain children
- Component definitions go in `/apps/typerefinery/components/forms/fields/{component}/.content.json`

### 2. Sling Model Pattern

**MANDATORY**: All form field components MUST have a Sling Model that extends `BaseFormComponent`.

```java
@Model(adaptables = {
    Resource.class,
    SlingHttpServletRequest.class
}, defaultInjectionStrategy = OPTIONAL)
@Exporter(name = "jackson", extensions = "json", options = {
    @ExporterOption(name = "SerializationFeature.WRITE_DATES_AS_TIMESTAMPS", value = "true")
})
public class YourComponent extends BaseFormComponent {
    
    protected static final String DEFAULT_MODULE = "yourcomponent";
    protected static final String DEFAULT_LABEL = "Your Label";
    protected static final String DEFAULT_PLACEHOLDER = "Your placeholder";
    
    @Inject
    @Getter
    @Default(values = "defaultValue")
    public String yourProperty;
    
    @Override
    @PostConstruct
    protected void init() {
        this.module = DEFAULT_MODULE;
        super.init();
        
        if (StringUtils.isBlank(label)) {
            this.label = DEFAULT_LABEL;
        }
        
        if (StringUtils.isBlank(placeholder)) {
            this.placeholder = DEFAULT_PLACEHOLDER;
        }
        
        style.addClasses("form-control");
    }
}
```

**Rules:**
- **REQUIRED**: Extend `ai.typerefinery.websight.models.components.forms.BaseFormComponent`
- **REQUIRED**: Use `@Model` with `Resource.class` and `SlingHttpServletRequest.class` as adaptables
- **REQUIRED**: Use `@Exporter` with `"jackson"` name and `"json"` extension
- **REQUIRED**: Override `init()` method, call `super.init()` first
- **REQUIRED**: Set `this.module` to component-specific module name
- **REQUIRED**: Use `@Inject`, `@Getter` (Lombok), and `@Default` for properties
- **REQUIRED**: Compute all conditional attributes and defaults in `init()` method
- **REQUIRED**: Use `{AttributeName}Attr` pattern for computed HTML attribute values
- Package: `ai.typerefinery.websight.models.components.forms`

**MANDATORY: Move All Logic to Model**

**CRITICAL RULE**: All business logic, defaults, conditionals, and attribute computations MUST be in the Sling Model's `@PostConstruct init()` method. Templates MUST only reference computed model properties.

**What Goes in Model:**
- ✅ All conditional logic (type checks, mode checks, state checks)
- ✅ All default values (fallbacks, empty string handling)
- ✅ All attribute value computations (type mapping, value formatting)
- ✅ All CSS class computations (conditional classes based on type/state)
- ✅ All boolean flag computations (should show, should hide, should mask)

**What Goes in Template:**
- ✅ Only direct property references: `${model.propertyName}`
- ✅ Only `data-sly-attribute` with computed properties: `data-sly-attribute.{attr}="${model.{attr}Attr}"`
- ✅ Simple attribute bindings: `id="${model.id}"`, `name="${model.name}"`

**Example: Computed Properties Pattern**

```java
// In Sling Model:
@Getter
private String typeAttr;        // Computed: HTML type attribute
@Getter
private String valueAttr;       // Computed: HTML value attribute with defaults
@Getter
private String placeholderAttr; // Computed: null if not applicable
@Getter
private Boolean requiredAttr;   // Computed: null if not applicable
@Getter
private Integer minAttr;        // Computed: null if not range type
@Getter
private String inputmaskAttr;   // Computed: null if masking not needed

@PostConstruct
protected void init() {
    super.init();
    
    // Compute all conditional attributes here
    this.typeAttr = computeTypeAttr();
    this.valueAttr = computeValueAttr();
    this.placeholderAttr = computePlaceholderAttr();
    this.requiredAttr = computeRequiredAttr();
    // ... etc
}
```

### 3. Template Structure

**MANDATORY**: Form field components MUST follow the standard template structure.

#### Main Template (`{component}.html`)

```html
<!--/* Copyright header */-->
<sly data-sly-use.model="ai.typerefinery.websight.models.components.forms.YourComponent">
  <div class="${model.componentClassNames}"> 
    <sly data-sly-use.template="./variant.html" data-sly-call="${template.variant @ model=model}">
    </sly>
  </div>
</sly>
```

**Rules:**
- **REQUIRED**: Adapt the component-specific Sling Model
- **REQUIRED**: Use `model.componentClassNames` for CSS classes
- **REQUIRED**: Include `variant.html` template via `data-sly-call`
- The base `field/variant.html` handles label wrapper - your variant provides the input element

#### Variant Template (`variant.html`)

**CRITICAL: VERY LEAN HTML SIGNATURE**

**MANDATORY RULE**: HTML templates MUST have the absolute minimum HTML signature possible. All logic, defaults, and conditional attributes MUST be computed in the Sling Model.

```html
<template data-sly-template.variant="${ @ model }">
  <input 
    component="${model.componentName}"
    isInput="true"
    id="${model.id}" 
    type="${model.typeAttr}"
    name="${model.name}"
    value="${model.valueAttr}"
    data-fieldId="${model.parentFieldId}" 
    data-model="${model.jsonString}"
    class="${model.variantClassNames}"
    data-sly-attribute.placeholder="${model.placeholderAttr}"
    data-sly-attribute.required="${model.requiredAttr}"
    data-sly-attribute.min="${model.minAttr}"
    data-sly-attribute.max="${model.maxAttr}"
    data-sly-attribute.step="${model.stepAttr}"
    data-sly-attribute.data-inputmask="${model.inputmaskAttr}"
    data-sly-attribute.disabled="${model.disabledAttr}"
  />
</template>
```

**MANDATORY Rules for Lean HTML Signatures:**

1. **NO CONDITIONALS IN TEMPLATES**: 
   - ❌ **FORBIDDEN**: `${model.inputType == 'rating' ? null : model.placeholder}`
   - ✅ **REQUIRED**: Compute `placeholderAttr` in model, use `model.placeholderAttr` directly

2. **NO DEFAULTS IN TEMPLATES**:
   - ❌ **FORBIDDEN**: `${model.value || '#000000'}`
   - ✅ **REQUIRED**: Compute `valueAttr` in model's `init()` method with defaults

3. **NO LOGIC IN TEMPLATES**:
   - ❌ **FORBIDDEN**: `${model.inputType != 'rating' && model.validationRequired}`
   - ✅ **REQUIRED**: Compute `requiredAttr` in model, use `model.requiredAttr` directly

4. **USE COMPUTED PROPERTIES**:
   - **REQUIRED**: Create computed properties in model with `{AttributeName}Attr` suffix pattern
   - **REQUIRED**: All conditional logic, defaults, and type mappings in `@PostConstruct init()` method
   - **REQUIRED**: Properties return `null` if attribute should not be rendered (use `data-sly-attribute`)

5. **USE DATA-MODEL FOR CLIENT-SIDE**:
   - **REQUIRED**: Always include `data-model="${model.jsonString}"` attribute
   - **REQUIRED**: Client-side JavaScript MUST read configuration from `data-model`, NOT from DOM queries
   - **FORBIDDEN**: Querying DOM for `data-*` attributes or element classes for configuration
   - **REQUIRED**: Parse `componentConfig` from `data-model` attribute using `componentNs.getComponentConfig()`

**Computed Property Pattern:**

For each HTML attribute that needs conditional logic or defaults, create a computed property in the model:

```java
/**
 * Computed: HTML {attribute} attribute value.
 * {Description of when it's null vs when it has a value}
 */
@Getter
private {Type} {attribute}Attr;

// In init() method:
if (condition) {
    this.{attribute}Attr = computedValue;
} else {
    this.{attribute}Attr = null; // Won't render attribute
}
```

**Template Usage:**

```html
<!-- Use data-sly-attribute to conditionally render attributes -->
data-sly-attribute.{attribute}="${model.{attribute}Attr}"
```

**Rules:**
- **REQUIRED**: Use `data-sly-template.variant` pattern
- **REQUIRED**: Include `component`, `id`, `name`, `data-fieldId`, `data-model` attributes
- **REQUIRED**: Use computed model properties (`{name}Attr`) for all conditional attributes
- **REQUIRED**: Include `data-model` with `model.jsonString` for client-side data access
- **REQUIRED**: All defaults and conditionals computed in model, not template
- **FORBIDDEN**: Ternary operators, `||` defaults, or conditionals in template expressions
- The base field component's variant handles label wrapper automatically

