- Parsys integration for child components
- JSON output compilation

## Best Practices

### 1. Lean HTML Signatures (MANDATORY)

**CRITICAL RULE**: HTML templates MUST have the absolute minimum signature possible.

**Rules:**
- **FORBIDDEN**: Conditionals, ternary operators, or `||` defaults in template expressions
- **REQUIRED**: All logic, defaults, and conditionals computed in Sling Model
- **REQUIRED**: Use computed `{AttributeName}Attr` properties for conditional attributes
- **REQUIRED**: Use `data-sly-attribute` with computed properties that return `null` when not applicable
- **REQUIRED**: Client-side JavaScript reads from `data-model`, NOT DOM queries
- **REQUIRED**: Pass `componentConfig` (from `data-model`) to all initialization functions

**Example Pattern:**
```java
// Model: Compute all logic
@Getter private String typeAttr;
@Getter private String valueAttr;

@PostConstruct
protected void init() {
    this.typeAttr = computeTypeAttr();  // All logic here
    this.valueAttr = computeValueAttr(); // All defaults here
}
```

```html
<!-- Template: Only property references -->
<input 
  type="${model.typeAttr}"
  value="${model.valueAttr}"
  data-model="${model.jsonString}"
/>
```

### 2. Reuse Shared Fragments

**REQUIRED**: Always use shared dialog fragments from `forms/form/common/` for consistency.

### 2. Follow Naming Conventions

- Component directory: lowercase, descriptive (e.g., `input`, `textarea`, `fileupload`)
- Sling Model class: PascalCase, matches component name (e.g., `Input`, `Textarea`, `FileUpload`)
- Module name: lowercase, matches component directory

### 4. CSS Classes

- Use Bootstrap classes where possible (`form-control`, `form-group`, etc.)
- Add component-specific classes via `style.addClasses()` in Sling Model
- Use `componentClassNames` for wrapper, `variantClassNames` for input element
- **REQUIRED**: Compute conditional classes in `init()` method, not template

### 4.1. CSS Namespacing (MANDATORY)

**CRITICAL**: All CSS selectors in component `style.css` files MUST be properly namespaced to prevent global conflicts.

**Rules:**
- **REQUIRED**: Scope all selectors to the component using `[component="{componentName}"]` attribute selector
- **REQUIRED**: Use component-prefixed class names (e.g., `.input-rating-items`, not `.rating-items`)
- **REQUIRED**: Namespace both custom classes and element selectors
- **FORBIDDEN**: Global selectors without component scope (e.g., `input[type="color"]` should be `[component="input"] input[type="color"]`)

**Pattern:**
```css
/* ✅ CORRECT: Namespaced */
[component="input"] input[type="color"].form-control-color {
  /* styles */
}

[component="input"] .input-rating-items {
  /* styles */
}

/* ❌ WRONG: Global selector */
input[type="color"].form-control-color {
  /* styles - can conflict with other components */
}

.rating-items {
  /* styles - global class name can conflict */
}
```

**Component Name:**
- Use the component name from `model.componentName` (e.g., `"input"`, `"button"`, `"select"`)
- This matches the `component` attribute in the HTML template

### 5. Default Values

- Always provide sensible defaults for required fields
- Use `@Default` annotation with appropriate default values for injected properties
- **MANDATORY**: Set all computed defaults in `init()` method (for `{attr}Attr` properties)
- **FORBIDDEN**: Defaults in template expressions (e.g., `${model.value || 'default'}`)

### 6. Use Data-Model for Client-Side Configuration

**MANDATORY**: Client-side JavaScript MUST read configuration from `data-model` attribute.

**Rules:**
- **REQUIRED**: Template includes `data-model="${model.jsonString}"` attribute
- **REQUIRED**: JavaScript uses `componentNs.getComponentConfig($component)` to parse
- **REQUIRED**: Pass `componentConfig` object to all initialization functions
- **FORBIDDEN**: DOM queries for configuration (e.g., `$component.find('input').attr('type')`)
- **FORBIDDEN**: Reading configuration from data attributes or element classes

**Example:**
```javascript
// ✅ REQUIRED: Read from data-model
const componentConfig = componentNs.getComponentConfig($component);
ns.initRating($component, componentConfig);

// ❌ FORBIDDEN: DOM queries
const type = $component.find('input').attr('type');
```

### 7. Documentation

**MANDATORY**: All form components MUST have a `README.md` file with:

1. **Component Overview** - Brief description of component purpose
2. **Information Section** - Component metadata including:
   - Component group, resourceType, title, description
   - **Showcase path** - Link to showcase page
   - Local code path
   - Source repository link
   - Readme link
3. **Authoring Section** - Dialog tabs and fields documentation
4. **Variants Section** - Component variants (if applicable)

**Showcase Path Format:**
```markdown
- **Showcase**: [/typerefinery/components/forms/{component}](https://cms.typerefinery.localhost:8101/apps/websight/index.html/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/{component}::editor)
```

