## Common Patterns

### Pattern 1: Simple Input Field

Extend base field, add type-specific properties, minimal customization.

**Example**: Input, Textarea, Radio

### Pattern 2: Complex Input Field

Extend base field, add clientlibs, event actions, variants.

**Example**: Button, FileUpload

### Pattern 3: Container Field

Extend base field, set `isContainer: true`, handle child components.

**Example**: Composite

## Showcase Examples

**MANDATORY**: When creating a new form component, you MUST also create showcase examples.

**CRITICAL RULE: MANDATORY Showcase Updates for Component Changes**

**MANDATORY**: Whenever ANY change is made to a component (new features, new properties, new variants, bug fixes, refactoring, CSS changes, JavaScript changes, etc.), the showcase page MUST be updated to demonstrate and validate those changes.

**Update Triggers (ALL MANDATORY):**
- ✅ **New features** added to component
- ✅ **New properties** added to dialog
- ✅ **New variants** created
- ✅ **Behavioral changes** (how component works)
- ✅ **CSS/styling changes** (visual appearance, namespacing)
- ✅ **JavaScript changes** (client-side behavior)
- ✅ **Bug fixes** that affect functionality or appearance
- ✅ **Refactoring** that changes component structure
- ✅ **New input types** or field types
- ✅ **Configuration changes** (new dialog fields, options)
- ✅ **Documentation updates** in README

**Showcase Update Requirements:**
1. **MANDATORY**: Add examples demonstrating the new/changed feature
2. **MANDATORY**: Test all showcase examples after changes
3. **MANDATORY**: Update README if component documentation changed
4. **MANDATORY**: Use container components to group related examples
5. **MANDATORY**: Include edge cases and different configurations
6. **MANDATORY**: Verify all existing examples still work correctly

**Examples:**
- Added new `rating` input type → Must add rating examples to showcase
- Added `rangeMin`, `rangeMax`, `rangeStep` properties → Must add range examples with different configurations
- Changed CSS namespacing → Must verify all showcase examples still work correctly
- Added custom icon classes for rating → Must add example showing custom icons
- Fixed bug in component behavior → Must verify fix works in showcase
- Refactored template → Must test all showcase examples still render correctly

**NO EXCEPTIONS**: Every component change MUST include showcase updates. This ensures:
- Features are properly demonstrated
- Changes are validated and tested
- Documentation stays current
- Users can see all available features
- Regression testing is performed

### Showcase Location

```
tests/content/src/main/content/jcr_root/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/{component}/
└── .content.xml
```

### Showcase Requirements

**REQUIRED**: Showcase pages MUST include:

1. **Basic Usage Example** - Simple, default component usage
2. **Variants** - If component has variants, show each variant
3. **Configuration Options** - Show different configuration options
4. **Integration Examples** - Show component working within forms
5. **Edge Cases** - Show validation, error states (if applicable)

### Updating Main Forms Showcase

**MANDATORY**: Update the main forms showcase page:
- `tests/content/src/main/content/jcr_root/content/typerefinery-showcase/pages/components/forms/.content.xml`
- Add your component examples to demonstrate usage
- Include variants and different configurations

### Showcase Best Practices

- **MANDATORY**: Use container components to group related examples
- Use `typerefinery/components/layout/container` with `variant="sectionwithtitle"` to create titled sections
- Group examples by feature/capability (e.g., "Basic Input Types", "Input with Validation", "Disabled States")
- Use clear, descriptive container titles that describe the grouped examples
- Each container should contain related examples demonstrating a specific feature or capability
- Use `flexEnabled="true"` on containers for responsive layout
- Include complete form examples, not just isolated components
- Show Flow integration when applicable
- Test all showcase examples before committing
- **CRITICAL: Each form field MUST have a unique `name` attribute** - Use `name="..."` (NOT `fieldName="..."`) in showcase XML
- **REQUIRED**: All showcase field examples must include `name="unique_field_name"` to ensure proper form submission
- **REQUIRED**: Use descriptive, unique names (e.g., `name="input_email"`, `name="rating_1_star"`, `name="input_color_basic"`)

**Container Pattern Example:**
```xml
<container_1
    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
    sling:resourceType="typerefinery/components/layout/container"
    flexEnabled="true"
    id="container_1_BASIC_TYPES"
    title="Basic Input Types"
    variant="sectionwithtitle">
    <input_1
        jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
        sling:resourceType="typerefinery/components/forms/input">
        <label
            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
            sling:resourceType="typerefinery/components/forms/fields/label"
            label="Enter Email Address"/>
        <field
            jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
            sling:resourceType="typerefinery/components/forms/fields/input"
            name="input_email"
            inputType="email"
            placeholder="Eg. test@example.com"/>
    </input_1>
</container_1>
```

**CRITICAL**: Notice the `name="input_email"` attribute - **ALWAYS use `name` (NOT `fieldName`)** and ensure each field has a unique name.

## Validation Checklist

Before submitting a new form component:

- [ ] Component extends `typerefinery/components/forms/field` via `sling:resourceSuperType`
- [ ] Sling Model extends `BaseFormComponent`
- [ ] Template uses standard pattern (`{component}.html` + `variant.html`)
- [ ] **HTML signature is VERY LEAN** - no conditionals, defaults, or logic in template
- [ ] **All logic computed in model** - conditionals, defaults, type mappings in `init()` method
- [ ] **Computed properties use `{AttributeName}Attr` pattern** - e.g., `typeAttr`, `valueAttr`
- [ ] **Template uses only property references** - `${model.property}` or `${model.{attr}Attr}`
- [ ] **Conditional attributes use `data-sly-attribute`** - with computed properties that return `null` when not applicable
- [ ] **Client-side reads from `data-model`** - uses `componentNs.getComponentConfig()`, not DOM queries
- [ ] Dialog uses shared fragments from `forms/form/common/`
- [ ] Component appears in "Typerefinery - Forms" group
- [ ] Component works with form's `getFormData()` function
- [ ] Component integrates with Flow API (when form has Flow enabled)
- [ ] Component follows naming conventions
- [ ] Component includes appropriate default values (in model, not template)
- [ ] **README.md created** with component documentation
- [ ] **README.md includes showcase path** to component showcase page
- [ ] **README.md includes component details** (overview, authoring, variants)
- [ ] **Showcase page created** at `tests/content/.../forms/{component}/.content.xml`
- [ ] **Showcase page uses container components** to group examples by feature/capability
- [ ] **Main showcase page updated** with component examples
- [ ] **MANDATORY: Showcase updated for ANY component changes** (features, properties, variants, bug fixes, CSS, JS, refactoring)
- [ ] **All showcase examples tested and working** after changes
- [ ] **CRITICAL: Each showcase field has unique `name` attribute** - Use `name="..."` (NOT `fieldName="..."`)
- [ ] **All field names are unique** - No duplicate `name` values across showcase examples

